        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The area becomes four times as large: a side length of $x\\text{ cm}$ gives $x^2\\text{ cm}^2$, while $2x\\text{ cm}$ gives $4x^2\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{original}}&=x^2\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=(2x)^2\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=4x^2\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$\nDoubling both dimensions makes four copies of the original square, so the area is four times as large.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p19-q18-a-solution-squares",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 19 question 18(a), authored solution illustration\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (1.5,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (1.5,1.5);\n\\coordinate (D) at (0,1.5);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;\n\\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$x\\text{ cm}$};\n\\path (A)--(D) node[midway,left] {$x\\text{ cm}$};\n\\path (A)--(C) node[midway] {$x^2$};\n\\coordinate (E) at (3,0);\n\\coordinate (F) at (6,0);\n\\coordinate (G) at (6,3);\n\\coordinate (H) at (3,3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (E)--(F)--(G)--(H)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (4.5,0)--(4.5,3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (3,1.5)--(6,1.5);\n\\path (E)--(F) node[midway,below] {$2x\\text{ cm}$};\n\\path (F)--(G) node[midway,right] {$2x\\text{ cm}$};\n\\node at (3.75,0.75) {$x^2$};\n\\node at (5.25,0.75) {$x^2$};\n\\node at (3.75,2.25) {$x^2$};\n\\node at (5.25,2.25) {$x^2$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
